   "subject": "Re: How to measure Latent means?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><code><span style=\"color:#606\">There</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> are multiple methods</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Here</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> one</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">See</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a SEM text such </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Kline</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> details</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># Reference group method</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>HS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;<br>  visual =~ c(l1, l1) * x1 + c(l2, l2) * x2 + c(l3, l3) * x3       # CFA model with loadings constrained across groups<br>  visual ~~ c(1, NA) * visual                                      # fix latent variable variance in first group<br>  visual ~ c(0, NA) * 1                                            # constrain latent variable mean to 1 in first group<br>  x1 ~~ x1<br>  x2 ~~ x2<br>  x3 ~~ x3<br>  x1 ~ c(v1, v1) * 1                                               # constrain intercepts across groups<br>  x2 ~ c(v2, v2) * 1<br>  x3 ~ c(v3, v3) * 1<br>&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># end model syntax</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">HS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>              data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">HolzingerSwineford1939</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>              </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;school&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                                    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># specify two-group analysis</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br>For a statistical test, rerun the model with both latent variable means set to zero and then inspect the chi-square difference test.<br><br><code><span style=\"color:#660\">------------------------</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Keith</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Markus</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">John</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Jay</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">College</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> of </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Criminal</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Justice</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> CUNY<br>http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426138321000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17bDHFTbVlfvtNRXwmiYhg\">jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus</a></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Frontiers</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> of </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Test</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Validity</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Theory</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Measurement</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Causation</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Meaning</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>http</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//<a href=\"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426138321000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vxetQZm2pG5cdYpNNIYMF\">www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/</a></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></code><br><br></div>"
